# toggle.zd — the two controls that are a button plus one ARIA state.
#
# Neither of these existed before `aria-checked` and `aria-pressed` were
# spellable, and neither is a compromise now that they are. That is the
# thing worth saying about this file: every other widget in this directory
# gives something up, and these two give up nothing.
#
# A switch and a toggle button are both a `button` the reader operates and
# a state the program holds. A `button` is focusable, is in the tab order,
# is operated by Enter and by Space, and needs no handler for any of that;
# nothing has to move focus, and the keystroke arrives at the control that
# is already focused. The one thing missing was a way to say what state the
# button is *in*, and a button that toggles something without announcing
# whether it is on is a control a reader can operate and never read.
#
# WHY TWO AND NOT ONE. They are announced differently and they mean
# different things. `role="switch"` with `aria-checked` is a setting that
# is on or off — it takes effect immediately and there is nothing to
# confirm. `aria-pressed` on a plain button is a button that stays down:
# the control is still a button, and what changed is the *view*, not a
# setting. Bold in a toolbar is pressed; "Notify me" is checked. §4.1's
# rule against two ways to write one thing is not touched, because these
# are two things.
#
# WHAT NEITHER DOES: nothing. There is no focus to move, no second element
# to point at, and no keyboard behaviour the browser does not already
# supply.

# A setting that is on or off.
#
# `setting` is the caller's `Truth` signal, and it is the whole state: the
# button reads it to announce itself and writes it when pressed, so there
# is no way for what is shown and what is held to disagree. The label is
# the button's own text, which is also its accessible name — a switch whose
# name lives in a separate element beside it is the arrangement that goes
# wrong when the two are read in the wrong order.
component Switch with label, setting, class
    Button label, class is class, role is "switch", checked is setting
        on click
            set setting to not setting

# A button that stays down.
#
# No role: it is a button, and `aria-pressed` is what says it is one with
# two states. Giving it `role="switch"` would announce a setting, and what
# this is is a command whose effect persists.
component ToggleButton with label, down, class
    Button label, class is class, pressed is down
        on click
            set down to not down
